<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Remove Varying Portion of Hard Prompts for Mistral</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We vary <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> from 10% to 60% and report the results in Figure <a href="#A4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix D Remove Varying Portion of Hard Prompts for Mistral ‣ On the Role of Difficult Prompts in Self-Play Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
There is an increasing trend as <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> grows from 10% to 60%, with the peak performance observed at <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=50\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
Beyond this point, removing a larger fraction of prompts begins to degrade performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05534v1/k_mistral.svg" id="A4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:264/169;" width="264" height="169"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>We present the performance of model on AlpacaEval 2 as we change <math id="A4.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> from 10 to 50 percent on Mistral. Performance first improve and then degrade as we prune more and more hard prompts.
Performance reaches peak when we remove about 50 percent of most difficult prompts.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
